    <artifactId>homing-ui-dialog</artifactId>
    <description>
        The dialog: a frame that owns the screen until dismissed - scrim,
        inert on everything else, keyboard capture, focus restore, an action
        row of the elements' buttons - or, non-modal, one that does not.
        openDialog(opts) returns a handle; the content is built into the
        dialog's own branch and dissolved with it. The modality is a
        headless module of its own, Modality, so that it can move into the
        component base once a second component holds a layer this way.
        Built fresh beside the studio's SystemDialog, whose contract it keeps.
    </description>
